### Enhancements

* Parse `MatchSpec` strings with the v3 parser for all solvers, instead of only for `rattler`. This keeps complete `extras` and `flags` lists (e.g. `httpx2[extras=[cli,http2]]` or `httpx2[extras=cli,http2]`) and accepts nested `when` expressions. (#16724 via #16906)

### Bug fixes

* Fix `InvalidMatchSpec` when parsing list-style `extras`/`flags` (e.g. `httpx2[extras=[cli,http2]]`)
  with solvers other than `rattler`. (#16724 via #16906)
* Fix `MatchSpec` silently dropping all but the first item of unquoted `extras`/`flags` lists (e.g.
  `httpx2[extras=cli,http2]`) with solvers other than `rattler`. (#16724 via #16906)
* Fix `MatchSpec` silently ignoring the version constraint in bracketed expressions without an `=`
  separator (e.g. `numpy[version<2]`) with solvers other than `rattler`. The constraint is now kept
  and a deprecation warning is emitted. (#16724 via #16906)

### Deprecations

* Mark `MatchSpec` version expressions in brackets without an `=` separator (e.g. `numpy[version<2]`)
  as pending deprecation; use `numpy[version='<2']` instead. (#16724 via #16906)

